 mergers took Belgium from 581 to 565 municipalities.","title":"REFNIS- en NUTS-nomenclaturen: wijzigingen van kracht vanaf 2 december 2024 en vanaf 1 januari 2025","url":"https://statbel.fgov.be/sites/default/files/files/opendata/Nuts/Note%20REFNIS-NUTS%202025-NL.pdf"},"statbel_sectors_2025":{"file":"sh_statbel_statistical_sectors_31370_20250101.geojson","publisher":"Statbel (Statistics Belgium)","role":"Municipality names and hierarchy. For nis_history: the old-to-new mapping, read from statistical sector codes whose five-digit prefix is the pre-merger NIS while the feature's cd_munty_refnis is the post-merger NIS.","title":"Statistical sectors of Belgium, situation 01/01/2025","url":"https://statbel.fgov.be/sites/default/files/files/opendata/Statistische%20sectoren/sh_statbel_statistical_sectors_31370_20250101.geojson.zip","vintage":"2025-01-01"},"walloon_decree_hainaut_arrondissements_2018":{"publisher":"Gouvernement wallon","role":"Explains the 11 records of kind \"recode\". No municipality changed; the arrondissements of Ath, Charleroi, Soignies, Thuin, Tournai and Mouscron were redrawn, the arrondissements of La Louvière and Tournai-Mouscron were created, and because the second digit of a NIS code is the arrondissement number, every affected municipality was renumbered.","title":"Arrêté du Gouvernement wallon du 25 janvier 2018 modifiant les limites de certains arrondissements administratifs du Hainaut, en vigueur au 1 janvier 2019"}}}
